<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!-- READ THIS BEFORE COUNTING ON THE RULE BELOW: as of Odoo 18 it does
         not run, and it cannot be made to run by fixing its domain.

         Every path the web client uses to fetch an action reads as superuser.
         In addons/web/controllers/action.py the /web/action/load endpoint does
         `Actions.browse([action_id]).sudo().read(['type'])`, then
         `request.env[action_type].sudo().browse([action_id])._get_action_dict()`,
         and ir_actions.py's own `_get_action_dict` does `self.sudo().read()[0]`.
         An ir.rule on ir.actions.client is bypassed at every one of them.
         ir.actions.client also has no groups_id field (only act_window and
         server do), so there is no built-in group gate for this model either.

         What actually keeps Property closed:

           * The menu tree. majal_real_estate.menu_majal_real_estate_root
             carries groups="majal_real_estate.group_majal_real_estate_user",
             and Odoo prunes the children of a menu the user cannot see. A user
             without the Property role has no Property menu at all.

           * The business-model ACLs and record rules. These are the
             authoritative data boundary and always were. A user who guesses a
             client action id can render an empty Property shell; every figure
             inside it is fetched through the ordinary model checks and comes
             back empty.

         The rule is kept rather than deleted because it costs nothing and
         would start working if Odoo ever stops sudo-ing that path. It is
         explicitly NOT load-bearing, and a security review should not record
         it as a control that is in force. -->
    <record id="rule_property_client_actions" model="ir.rule">
        <field name="name">Property client actions require Property access (inert on Odoo 18 -- see comment)</field>
        <field name="model_id" ref="base.model_ir_actions_client"/>
        <field name="global" eval="True"/>
        <field name="domain_force">[(1, '=', 1)] if user.has_group('majal_real_estate.group_majal_real_estate_user') else [('tag', 'not in', ['majal_property_ui.property_home', 'construction_ui.workspace.property_portfolio', 'construction_ui.workspace.unit_inventory', 'construction_ui.workspace.reservations', 'construction_ui.workspace.leads', 'construction_ui.workspace.installments', 'construction_ui.workspace.commissions', 'construction_ui.workspace.handovers', 'construction_ui.workspace.leases', 'construction_ui.workspace.rent_collection', 'construction_ui.workspace.unit_requests'])]</field>
    </record>
</odoo>
